CIMMYT Fertilizer Game
======================

This software is a derivative work. It is based on the MIT-licensed
"Investment Game" developed by the Alliance of Bioversity International and
CIAT, and IFPRI (the original GEF maize bundling field experiment). The
original code is used under the terms of the MIT License (see LICENSE), which
permits modification and redistribution provided the original copyright notice
and permission notice are retained.

Modifications by the International Maize and Wheat Improvement Center (CIMMYT)
adapt the game into a fertilizer risk-communication experiment (the "v2"
design): the in-game display × training arm was removed, game exposure itself
is the treatment (assigned outside the app), uncertainty is always shown as the
full icon-array distribution, probability-comprehension training runs for every
participant, and the round structure is 1 practice + 10 incentivized seasons.

This project is deployed independently of the upstream organization, on
CIMMYT-owned infrastructure (its own Cloudflare account, Pages project, Worker,
and Neon database). It shares no deployment, credentials, or data store with
the original.

